1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:02,020
The Prophet (peace be upon him) said:

2
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:03,780
“Present your ruqyahs to me.”

3
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:05,660
So what is the story behind this sentence?

4
00:00:06,210 --> 00:00:09,000
In the Jahiliyyah, people used to perform ruqyah with words that contained shirk.

5
00:00:09,370 --> 00:00:10,400
When Islam came,

6
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:13,610
the family of ‘Amr ibn Hazm came to the Prophet (peace be upon him)

7
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:14,350
and said:

8
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:16,890
“We have a ruqyah we use for scorpion stings.”

9
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,120
They presented it to him,

10
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:20,260
and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said:

11
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,570
“I see no harm in it.

12
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:24,640
Whoever among you can benefit his brother, let him do so.”

13
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:25,640
(Narrated by Muslim)

14
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:27,460
In another narration he said:

15
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:30,030
“There is no harm in ruqyah as long as it contains no shirk.”

16
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:31,600
This is the criterion:

17
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:35,170
every ruqyah that has no shirk and no unknown words

18
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:35,950
is permissible,

19
00:00:36,290 --> 00:00:38,410
and every ruqyah that contains shirk or cryptic charms

20
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:39,490
is rejected.

21
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,450
So measure what you hear against the Qur’an and the Sunnah,

22
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:44,170
and do not accept words you do not understand.

23
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:47,720
Share this clip with someone you love, and follow the channel.

